hw/scr/ - Vivado batch scripts
==============================

Tcl driven headless (vivado -mode batch), so the whole FPGA flow is
scriptable and diffable - no GUI, no project files checked in.

    build.tcl     read rtl/*.vhd (VHDL-2008) + the BOARD's con/*.xdc, run
                  synth + implementation + write_bitstream. Args: BOARD.
                  Output: build/vivado/<top>_<board>.bit
    program.tcl   open the hw_server, find the FPGA, download a .bit. Args:
                  path to the bitstream.

Invoked by hw.mk:
    make -f hw.mk bit  BOARD=basys3     # build.tcl
    make -f hw.mk prog                  # program.tcl

Vivado is not packaged in flake.nix (proprietary). For flashing without it,
use `make -f hw.mk prog-ofl` (openFPGALoader).
